The code statements that lead to the bug are:
ret = cx88_alsa_dma_map(chip);
ret = cx88_risc_databuffer(chip->pci, &buf->risc, buf->sglist,
				   chip->period_size, chip->num_periods, 1);
if (ret < 0)
    goto error;
Reason:
After `cx88_alsa_dma_map()` succeeds, if `cx88_risc_databuffer()` fails, the error path jumps directly to `error` without first calling `cx88_alsa_dma_unmap()`. This leaks the DMA mapping resources.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
if (ret < 0) {
    cx88_alsa_dma_unmap(chip);
    goto error;
}
Reason:
By adding `cx88_alsa_dma_unmap(chip)` inside the failure branch of `cx88_risc_databuffer()`, the DMA mapping is properly released before jumping to the `error` label, preventing the resource leak.

